# Stop orders wait until the last trade reaches their stop price, then become market orders, or limit orders for
# stop-limits.
> add ACME
added ACME
> sell 100 @ 101.00
ACME #1 SELL 100 @ 101.00 -> resting 100
> sell 100 @ 102.00
ACME #2 SELL 100 @ 102.00 -> resting 100
> buy 100 @ 99.00
ACME #3 BUY 100 @ 99.00 -> resting 100
> stop buy 50 @ 101.00
ACME #4 STOP BUY 50 @ 101.00 -> waiting for a trade at 101.00
> stop sell 30 @ 99.50 limit 99.00
ACME #5 STOP-LIMIT SELL 30 @ 99.50 limit 99.00 -> waiting for a trade at 99.50
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last -  resting 3  stops 2
              BID                       ASK
      99.00 x 100     (1)      101.00 x 100     (1)
                               102.00 x 100     (1)

# A trade at 101.00 triggers the buy stop. It buys 50 at market: 40 more at 101.00, then 10 at 102.00.
> buy 60 @ 101.00
ACME #6 BUY 60 @ 101.00 -> filled 60
  trade #1  60 @ 101.00  buy #6  sell #1
  trade #2  40 @ 101.00  buy #4  sell #1
  trade #3  10 @ 102.00  buy #4  sell #2
  stop #4 triggered
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last 102.00  resting 2  stops 1
              BID                       ASK
      99.00 x 100     (1)      102.00 x 90      (1)

# A trade at 99.00 triggers the sell stop-limit, which sells 30 at 99.00 or better.
> sell 10 @ 99.00
ACME #7 SELL 10 @ 99.00 -> filled 10
  trade #4  10 @ 99.00  buy #3  sell #7
  trade #5  30 @ 99.00  buy #3  sell #5
  stop #5 triggered
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last 99.00  resting 2
              BID                       ASK
      99.00 x 60      (1)      102.00 x 90      (1)
